hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20948","Affan narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan, Amr ibn Taghlib narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, received something and gave people and left people, and Jarir said: He gave men and left men. He said: It reached him that those he left blamed and said. He said: He ascended the pulpit and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: I give people and leave people, and I give men and leave men. Affan said: He said: This and this, and those I leave are dearer to me than those I give. I give people for what is in their hearts of panic and greed, and I entrust people to what Allah has placed in their hearts of richness and good, among them Amr ibn Taghlib. He said: I was sitting facing the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: I would not love to have for the word of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, red camels."
"20949","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan, he said: Amr ibn Taghlib narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I give peoples and turn away others, and those I leave are dearer to me than those I give. I give peoples for what I fear of their greed. He said: And I entrust peoples to what Allah, mighty and majestic, has placed in their hearts of richness and good, among them Amr ibn Taghlib. He said: Amr said: By Allah, I would not love to have for the word of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, red camels."
"20950","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Amr ibn Taghlib narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will fight before the Hour a people wearing hair, and you will surely fight a people as if their faces are hammered shields."
"20951","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, Amr ibn Taghlib narrated to us, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Among the signs of the Hour is that you fight a people broad-faced as if their faces are hammered shields."
"20952","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us from al-Hasan from Amr ibn Taghlib who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the signs of the Hour is that you fight peoples wearing hair."
"20953","Affan narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan, Amr ibn Taghlib narrated to us, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Among the signs of the Hour is that you fight a people whose sandals are hair, or wearing hair, and among the signs of the Hour is that you fight a people broad-faced as if their faces are hammered shields."
